--- !u!114 &810501276
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 810501266}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2bf080be06a0e604cb9cf97b1f099a15, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: SafeHaven::QuestGiver
  quest: {fileID: 0}
  greeting: 
  waitingLines:
    lines: []
    order: 0
  turnInText: 
  afterLines:
    lines: []
    order: 0
  showMarker: 1
  offers: []
  sideOffers:
  - quest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 561a591e33a3afa43894a23c9a44579f, type: 2}
    text: We always need firewood. Take this axe; there are good trees on the slope north of the road. Six logs will do us. It splits other things too, in case you need it to.
    acceptText: I'll bring wood.
    waitingText: Six logs from the slope north of the road. Walk up to a tree with the axe in hand and get chopping.
    askText: Do you need firewood?
    thanksText: That will keep us warm. Keep the axe.
  - quest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: ee58d4932a0cf6648ad82ee55f48f193, type: 2}
    text: Now that is a fine idea. Anything but this porridge. Here is a rod and a handful of grubs, and the lake is just south of the road. Two fish, and I'll owe you.
    acceptText: I'll go fishing.
    waitingText: Two fish from the lake. Hold attack to swing back, let go to cast, and strike when the float goes under.
    askText: Shall I catch us some fish?
    thanksText: Breakfast! You may be the best person on this expedition. Keep the rod; there is bound to be water in those woods.
  - quest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 94b700836e0b3024c8d665b28ccf4831, type: 2}
    text: Before you go in? Gladly. There is a dummy over there; hit it until your arm knows the way. Then I'll find you something that hits back, and we will see whether you can keep your teeth.
    acceptText: Show me.
    waitingText: 'Dummy first, then the rootling. Watch its shoulders: the blow is coming when they drop.'
    askText: Show me how to use this.
    thanksText: You'll do. Better than most I have trained, worse than you will be. Take these; you will want them.
  speakerName: Eirik
  portrait: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueCameraDistance: 0.65
